{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789894113,"nonce":"YIP9LmhrspROkowvgROo/ZgJnao=","title":"an untyped parameter is Dynamic, and arithmetic on it runs on the box pointer","message":"`extern inline function S(X, n) { return (X \u003e\u003e\u003e n) | (X \u003c\u003c (32 - n)); }` (haxe.crypto.Sha256, also Md5 and the `safeAdd`/`Ch`/`Maj` helpers) lowers with `*void` parameters; the body shifts and ors the POINTER bits, and `S(0x12345678, 4)` prints -6179975476677705718. Haxe infers such a parameter as a monomorph bound by its uses (Int here). `Sha256.encode(\"abc\")` faults in `doEncode`; `Sha1` happens to work because its helpers annotate `:Int`. Either infer the parameter type from its body (bit ops force Int) or, at minimum, unbox a Dynamic operand of an arithmetic/bit operator when the other operand is an Int, as the Optional case now does.","files":null}]}